# Linear project Swarm — TODO tracking

Track implementation work for this repo in **Linear**, not only in chat or local notes.

## Where

| Source | Use |
|--------|-----|
| **Linear** | [Project Swarm](https://linear.app/anhadhs-personal-workspace/project/swarm-929078a35985) — statuses, ownership, what’s done |
| **`docs/TODO.md`** | Long-form design, checklists, and “out of scope” — link from Linear issues |

Team: **Anhadh's Personal Workspace** (`ANH`). Project name: **Swarm**.

## When to touch Linear

- At the **start** of a multi-step or non-trivial swarm task: `list_issues` filtered by project **Swarm**; read `docs/TODO.md`.
- When you **finish** work that maps to a tracked item: move the issue to **Done** (or **Canceled** with a short reason).
- When you discover **new** follow-up work: create an issue in **Swarm** instead of only appending to chat.
- When the user asks about progress or TODOs: answer from Linear + `docs/TODO.md`, then update Linear if stale.

## Issue hygiene

- **One issue ≈ one deliverable** (e.g. one checklist row in `docs/TODO.md`), not an entire epic in the title.
- **Description**: 1–3 sentences + pointer to file/section (e.g. `docs/TODO.md` → Agent identity checklist item 1).
- **Statuses**: `Todo` / `Backlog` (not started), `In Progress` (active this session), `Done` (merged or verified), `Canceled` / `Duplicate` when appropriate.
- Do **not** paste secrets (tokens, `.env`) into Linear.

## Sync with `docs/TODO.md`

- If an unchecked checklist item has **no** matching Linear issue, create one in **Swarm** when you begin or when grooming TODOs.
- When a checklist item is **done**, check the box in `docs/TODO.md` **and** mark the Linear issue **Done** in the same change session when the user expects both kept in sync.
- Large architecture stays in `docs/TODO.md`; Linear holds **actionable** tasks.

## MCP

Use the **Linear** MCP tools (`list_issues`, `save_issue`, `list_comments`, etc.) with `project: "Swarm"` and team **ANH** as needed.